``` IX-04 | Partition Approaching minFreeSpace: Indexing About to Pause
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Warn before splunkd pauses indexing on a peer because a
    partition is approaching the minFreeSpace threshold, and confirm whether
    indexing has already stopped.
    Run on: SH.
    Query: Has indexing already paused (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/IX-04-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=splunkd earliest=-24h
    ("minFreeSpace" OR "paused" OR "disk space")
    (log_level=WARN OR log_level=ERROR)
| rex field=_raw "\]\s+-\s+(?<msg>.+)$"
| stats count earliest(_time) as first_seen latest(_time) as last_seen
        by host component msg
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - last_seen
